  note    = {Decision 9.39, the only brain:plasma measurement found for guanfacine and the test of the owner's dates reading. Quoted: "Measurement of guanfacine levels concurrently in both plasma and brain showed that guanfacine had higher brain than plasma levels and that the brain levels were fairly constant over the 3 h measured. Brain:plasma ratios were 2.1:1, 5.3:1 and 13.6:1 after 15, 90 and 180 min respectively." Also reports an octanol/buffer partition coefficient of 21.2 at pH 7.4. Read from the Consensus MCP abstract and confirmed against the Wiley Scholar Gateway full-text index, 15 October 2026; Wiley holds the abstract only for this article (total_chunks 1, not open access), so the methods could not be checked for perfusion, n or assay. Not usable as a partition coefficient: the ratio rises across all three timepoints, so no steady state is established}
}

